# liblastfm isn't a dependency any more - Last.fm scrobbling talks directly
# to the web service API now (src/internet/lastfm/lastfmws.*), since
# liblastfm has no Qt6 build anywhere. libmygpo-qt has no Qt6 build either;
# gpodder sync falls back to the vendored 3rdparty/libmygpo-qt5 copy - see
# CMakeLists.txt.
#
# qt6-5compat-dev is Debian's package name for Qt6's Core5Compat module;
# Ubuntu (jammy/noble/resolute) instead calls it libqt6core5compat6-dev -
# see the per-distro install lists in .github/workflows/all.yml, which are
# what actually drives each CI build (dpkg-buildpackage's -d flag skips
# Build-Depends checking here, so this listing doesn't gate the build).
